{:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329541} {:answer/id #uuid "6078ce66-cc65-5238-949b-cb37333f23f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25da20c-d3ef-5fc8-81ba-05bd7f23f551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329538} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa103db-8fe3-5e4f-8786-3e8e80d954e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca279526-b62e-56f6-bb58-940f0a3d4e3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94091" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-4){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-4){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2d495e-83ac-563a-923b-53a5c84064b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329545} {:answer/id #uuid "e80e3f9b-abf4-5061-a3cb-cb6a316f512a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329546} {:answer/id #uuid "7b822a13-e1cd-5b45-a763-dea8f050c727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329547} {:answer/id #uuid "443c69da-b249-5213-9d76-08b710b0adb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329548} {:answer/id #uuid "4de100ce-2821-5bc3-97a8-6959a5be99f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab2d495e-83ac-563a-923b-53a5c84064b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329545} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb8504f8-efb6-527b-a920-e7711490f632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc073d63-fb25-5413-bfbf-32bd918e2a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94093" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(3){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16295f87-f043-5952-9837-8078f1fd4b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329552} {:answer/id #uuid "22e05f01-6033-53e4-9bf4-c9988ba8813a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329553} {:answer/id #uuid "603edd03-6654-55e1-a27b-c98cc1588875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329554} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc25e35-105d-50c5-903d-d3f8deeea081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329555} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef13af9-e8e5-580d-8dba-52d8cfa05f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc25e35-105d-50c5-903d-d3f8deeea081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329555} :answer-field/id #uuid "186fcce2-a80a-55cf-a52e-be3e630037e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f71c8acd-e0e8-5ba6-aaaa-b92c7ebe1f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94097" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}({x}_{2})+{x}_{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040479e5-25ec-5676-bbce-1aa2605ad696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329559} {:answer/id #uuid "f3afea29-76bf-53da-b097-4e6919fe33d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329560} {:answer/id #uuid "df53b4e1-73c7-559e-8e9e-e3bec20db4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329561} {:answer/id #uuid "2aca9a51-de98-5c41-a605-9ea5c9e892c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329562} {:answer/id #uuid "efc46c75-a656-55a4-b149-c2222a66d8d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aca9a51-de98-5c41-a605-9ea5c9e892c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329562} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dc42ddc-34f1-5034-836c-3adc338e1693" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa520ceb-dcfd-527f-b050-d283d140e1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-94105" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1})+{x}_{2}(2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468de98b-2887-587d-a6fa-08d26cc2698f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329566} {:answer/id #uuid "b228d77c-27e0-5201-9c57-5006fcd29a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329567} {:answer/id #uuid "fd023245-7d38-5d14-8c27-987720c5b682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329568} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ccb8f0-378b-5d03-9301-84e98e4ead04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329569} {:answer/id #uuid "2a372720-df66-53cc-b3f0-60ca15197bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a372720-df66-53cc-b3f0-60ca15197bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329570} :answer-field/id #uuid "003f5cc2-2265-518b-ada2-7b58607dfed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1963362a-57e4-5a67-b932-bddf81aa4778" :question/math-academy-id "q-94113" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{-6}{2}=-3\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=-3$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=-3+1=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "056015f0-7d16-5ce3-b267-b04635ba752d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329573} {:answer/id #uuid "038cdf04-77a7-58e9-b409-e9bef0ad24fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329574} {:answer/id #uuid "2f11831a-adf6-54e9-864b-37bbc5b01056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329575} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbc3c5f-0d0f-5b40-b202-79d411761490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329576} {:answer/id #uuid "48349de2-172f-555d-9f36-f639631e6ec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbc3c5f-0d0f-5b40-b202-79d411761490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd1b039-6ff2-5677-b5d9-c6b88d9fc65c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c483845a-2df2-5f96-9a60-d364acbd9e17" :question/math-academy-id "q-94115" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=1$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=1-2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba0d6865-12de-5d9d-a477-0a9ebe66afd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329580} {:answer/id #uuid "c838e8e0-61e6-5e60-992a-6525732217bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329581} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1cdb0d-2b51-545f-9cf2-3d813f766c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329582} {:answer/id #uuid "39114c83-642b-5d04-971f-869f3c2701c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329583} {:answer/id #uuid "489266df-1d0d-55db-b1cf-815a04a49632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd1cdb0d-2b51-545f-9cf2-3d813f766c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329582} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b53e7f8-75d3-51ee-8786-fd4ba3663cc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48eb3bee-71af-55b4-ac22-cbdbf3fba67b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94117" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-5){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-10}{2}=-5.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(-5)+3=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad421802-26c1-5213-a10b-0799186bb9f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329587} {:answer/id #uuid "6abcc35c-70c0-5fa1-a95f-2a4fb9fa1d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329588} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7617e3-4e91-534b-9b04-ad0ec22a32cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329589} {:answer/id #uuid "9584e14a-6f16-5a85-b581-df59746a2262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329590} {:answer/id #uuid "35b4cf85-c620-50e4-95c9-bf79b02d4f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35b4cf85-c620-50e4-95c9-bf79b02d4f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329591} :answer-field/id #uuid "9445d247-8f3a-5484-a910-6509dafb73e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "073c0684-1181-52f2-8694-1c9e7ffaf10c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94120" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & b \\\\ 6 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,6{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{12}{2}=6,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-4}{2}=-2.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+0=-1.\n$$"}]}
